      <h2>Why Coastal Crosby Needs a Specialist</h2>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        <p>Crosby is one of the most well-off parts of north Merseyside. It has large seafront homes in Blundellsands and whole streets of 1930s family semis.</p>

        <p>What makes Crosby different from inland Liverpool is the salt air. Homes on Hall Road, Mariners Road, Burbo Bank Road South and the seafront are a few hundred metres from the Irish Sea. Outside boiler flues, condensate pipes, outside taps and bare copper pipes rust much faster here than inland.</p>

        <p>So a boiler flue may need replacing sooner on the coast. A damaged flue is a carbon monoxide risk. We check the flue on every boiler service. If you see rust streaks below the flue on your outside wall, call us straight away.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange" style="margin-top:1rem;">
