      <div class="pf-who-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">1</span><div><strong>Find the stopcock and turn it off</strong><p>For any leak, turn off the stopcock first. In most Crosby semis, it is under the kitchen sink. In Blundellsands detached homes, it is often in a utility room or basement. In the seafront flats, it is usually in the airing cupboard. Turn it clockwise to stop the water.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">2</span><div><strong>If you smell gas, get out</strong><p>Do not touch any switches. Open the windows as you leave. Call <a href="https://cadentgas.com/emergencies" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#c2410c;font-weight:700;">Cadent Gas on 0800 111 999</a> first. Once they have made it safe, call us on 0151 558 0334.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">3</span><div><strong>No heating? Check the pressure gauge</strong><p>Look at the gauge on the boiler. It should read 1 to 1.5 bar. If it is below 1 bar, top it up with the filling loop under the boiler. This often gets the heating back on. If it does not, call us.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-who-item pf-who-yes"><span class="pf-who-icon">4</span><div><strong>Photograph the damage</strong><p>Take photos and video before you clean up. Your insurer will want to see them. We can also write a leak report with photos for your insurer.</p></div></div>
