      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>The first hour is £120 on weekdays, 9am to 4pm. It is £150 on weekday evenings, nights and weekends. It is £180 on bank holidays. There is no call-out fee. Parts are at cost. If the job needs more time, we price it before we carry on. You get a written price before we start.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>We guarantee a 30 minute response across Crosby L23. A real person answers the phone, day or night. We send an engineer as soon as you call.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">COASTAL</span>&nbsp; Does being near the sea cause more plumbing problems in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Homes near the sea in Crosby rust faster. This hits outside pipes, boiler flues, condensate pipes and outside taps. Salt air and damp speed up the rust. Homes near Crosby Beach on Hall Road, Mariners Road and Burbo Bank Road South are worst hit. If you see rust stains on the flue outside, call us straight away. A damaged flue is a carbon monoxide risk.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">BLUNDELLSANDS</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Blundellsands seafront properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. We know the large detached homes on Warren Road, St Andrews Road, Anthonys Road and The Serpentine well. They often have several bathrooms, unvented cylinders, underfloor heating and high-end fittings. We are G3 qualified for unvented cylinder work. We carry common spares for premium brands.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">APARTMENTS</span>&nbsp; Do you work on Crosby's coastal apartment blocks?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Burbo Mansions, Gaywood Court, Fountain Court and the other seafront blocks have shared water and heating systems. We work with the managing agents when we need to reach risers or pump rooms. Flats cost the same fixed rates.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">PERIOD</span>&nbsp; Can you handle period property plumbing in Crosby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Crosby's Victorian and Edwardian homes date from the 1850s onwards. Some still have lead pipes and cast iron column radiators. We carry replacement parts and work around the original features. The old stone cottages in Little Crosby village need extra care, and we always give it.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Our Gas Safe registered engineers do all our gas work. By law, anyone doing gas work must be on the Gas Safe Register. You can check our registration at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. We give you the right paperwork for any gas work we do.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job has a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back and fix it free.</p></div></details>
